## Context

PR #541 (ticket 0310) registered the `adherence` pytest marker in this repo for
the first time — the worktree-predicate ratchet runs under it. The /gaze panel
on #541 flagged the gap: nothing wires the tier. `coding-python.md` prescribes
`make lint` running `-m adherence` and `make check-fast` excluding it; this
repo's Makefile has neither, so adherence tests run only inside the full
`make check` sweep and the fast loop's tier boundary is undeclared.

## Actions

1. Add a `lint` target running the adherence tier (`-m adherence`).
2. Exclude `-m adherence` (and any other slow tiers this repo uses) from the
   fast target, per the tiering table in `rules/coding-python.md`.
3. Verify `make check` still runs everything.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `make lint` runs the adherence tier only
- [ ] The fast tier excludes adherence tests
- [ ] `make check` coverage unchanged
